## Critical architecture: Hermes Agent integration
Hermes Agent (https://github.com/nousresearch/hermes-agent) is an autonomous agent runtime with built-in self-improvement via **Skills** (procedural memory in markdown files at `~/.hermes/skills/<category>/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter). Agent auto-creates skills after 5+ tool-call workflows, then improves them on subsequent runs.
**helios integrates with Hermes via MCP server** (Model Context Protocol). Register in `~/.hermes/config.yaml`:
```yaml
mcp_servers:
  helios:
    command: "uv"
    args: ["run", "helios-mcp"]
    tools:
      include: [get_recent_trades, get_strategy_config, get_goals, query_backtest,
                get_paper_results, list_hypotheses, get_shadow_test_status,
                propose_strategy_change, submit_journal_note, get_trade_analyses,
                append_trade_analysis]
Two separable deployments:

helios/ — Python trading runtime (Redis bus, signal modules, risk engine, broker adapter, composer, multi-cadence analyzer, FastAPI dashboard, MCP server). Lives in Docker stack. Runs continuously.
Hermes Agent — separate process, installed via Nous's install script. Scheduled meta-loop reads/writes to helios via MCP. Self-improves its skills over time.
Self-improvement gating is in helios, NOT Hermes. When Hermes proposes a strategy change via propose_strategy_change MCP tool, helios writes it to hypotheses table with status pending. Promotion to active requires either user dashboard approval OR a shadow-test outcome with statistical significance. Hermes never directly mutates risk limits, kill switches, or live execution — those tools are not exposed in the MCP server.

Multi-cadence trade analysis (non-negotiable, first-class)
Each trade is analyzed many times. Schema:

TradeAnalysis(
  trade_id, pass_kind ENUM[entry, in_flight, exit, eod, eow, eom, eoq],
  timestamp, analyzer_skill, text_md, features_referenced,
  hypotheses_generated, confidence_delta
)
Internal scheduler runs entry/in_flight/exit passes; Hermes cron runs eod/eow/eom/eoq passes. Each pass reads all prior passes for that trade plus market context. Exposed via MCP so Hermes skills can call get_trade_analyses(trade_id) and append_trade_analysis(...). Hypotheses generated by any pass go to the central hypothesis registry.

Three modes
YOLO: composer→risk→execution, no human in loop, audit log only
Approve-Critical: human approves trades above $ threshold OR risk-score above threshold (configurable)
Ask: every trade requires human approval
Approvals UI in dashboard; mobile push via Telegram bot for fast approvals.

